Students Parents and Families ROTC & Veterans Alumni (opens in new window/tab) Corporate Sponsors Donors Print Find It Fast Panel Close Panel Visit Apply Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Campus Map Search Clear Search About Directory (opens in new window/tab) myMU (opens in new window/tab) Athletics (opens in new window/tab) Map Jobs at MU Library Virtual Experience (opens in new window/tab) Financial Aid & Tuition Make a Gift Upcoming Events All Events Oct 17 Open House all day Oct 19 Classes Resume; Second Subterm Begins 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 30 PM N/A Oct 26 Advisement Period 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 27 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 28 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 29 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Latest News More News Post RSS Feeds Subscribe to Post Alerts Misericordia University Dean Presents at tecBRIDGE Innovation Conference 9 / 4 / 2026 9 : 26 AM Misericordia University Bridge Program Helps First-Year Students Prepare for College Success 9 / 3 / 2026 1 : 04 PM Misericordia University Expands Nursing Pathways as Pennsylvania Addresses Workforce Shortage 9 / 2 / 2026 10 : 51 AM Misericordia University Celebrates Convocation and Welcomes the Class of 2030 8 / 28 / 2026 2 : 06 PM Misericordia University Professor Selected for UC Berkeley Bridging Differences Fellowship 8 / 13 / 2026 10 : 03 AM Misericordia University Appoints Two New Members to Board of Trustees 7 / 30 / 2026 12 : 09 PM Admissions FAQ's More FAQ's What are the admission requirements? What type of financial aid is available? When should I apply? Who can I contact with questions about my application? What are the admission requirements? MU typically likes to see students with a history of proven success in the classroom with a minimum high school grade point average of 2.5. Minimum *SAT requirement is typically an 850 (Math + Critical Reading), but other factors can be taken into consideration. A number of programs have requirements for direct entry that are higher than university minimums. We advise checking the admission requirements for your program of interest within its designated section of the website. View our list of majors to find your program. *Note: Misericordia will be Test-Optional for Fall 2021 Admissions What type of financial aid is available? Misericordia offers merit-based scholarships for academics as well as community involvement, and need-based awards which can total well over $20,000 per year for qualified students. Visit our Financial Aid page to learn more . When should I apply? MU has a rolling admissions cycle, but we advise that students apply early in the cycle (Fall) as the space available in certain programs can be limited. Visit our Apply page to submit an application . Who can I contact with questions about my application? Your admissions counselor, or the Admissions Office at admiss@misericordia.edu or 1-866-262-6363. View our list of Admissions Staff to find your counselor. Dean of Students Callie Rimpfel Mack Dean of Students Phone: (570) 674-8318 Email: cmack@misericordia.edu Callie Rimpfel Mack, Dean of Students, works closely with Amy Lahart, Vice President for Mission and Student Success, to manage and carry out the mission and values of the Division for Mission Integration and Student Life. Callie Mack provides oversight for and assists the following departments with support for students' wellbeing: Community Standards (Student Conduct) Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS) New Student and Family Programs Student Health Services The Dean of Students is an advocate for students. She assists parents and families in supporting their students through various issues which may impact their success. She connects students and their families to various on and off campus resources to promote well-being and academic progress and success. Callie challenges and supports students to live the charisms of mercy, service, justice and hospitality both individually and collectively as a Misericordia University community. Finally, the Dean of Students is a resource person for students who report behaviors prohibited by the University's Sexual Harassment & Sexual Misconduct Policy or who are involved in investigations related to this Policy. Staff Important Links Staff Callie Rimpfel Mack Dean of Students 107 Banks Student Life Center cmack@misericordia.edu (570)674-8318 Dana Fortunato Pavlick Manager for Student Wellness and Conduct 128 Banks Student Life Center dpavlick@misericordia.edu - Dana Fortunato Pavlick, MS, LPC serves as the Manager of Student Wellness and Conduct out of Misericordia’s Dean of Students Office. She serves as one of campus’s conduct officers and is responsible for many wellness initiatives all over campus. Previous to holding this position, Dana received her Master's Degree from The University of Scranton in Clinical Mental Health Counseling and worked in clinical settings as a licensed professional counselor for over 6 years before transitioning to her current position in higher education. Dana remains an avid advocate for mental health on and off campus and approaches student care with a holistic lens that aligns with Misericordia’s Core Values of Mercy, Service, Justice and Hospitality. Kimberly Caffrey Executive Assistant to the VP for Mission and Student Success kcaffery@misericordia.edu Important Links Student Handbook File an Incident Report Sexual Misconduct and Title IX Sexual Harassment Information Sexual Misconduct and Title IX Sexual Harassment Policy Community Standards Misericordia University Founded by the Sisters of Mercy 301 Lake Street, Dallas , PA 18612 (570) 674-6400 Helpful Links Full-Time Undergraduate Online Programs Accelerated Degrees Jobs at MU Part-Time Graduate Open Houses Make a Gift to MU TikTok (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) Facebook (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) LinkedIn (opens in new window/tab) Privacy Policy (opens in new window/tab) Site Map Accessibility Back to top Powered by Finalsite"
