ersity Camps Other Offices Athletics Information For Future Students Parents and Families ROTC & Veterans Alumni (opens in new window/tab) Corporate Sponsors Donors Print Find It Fast Panel Close Panel Visit Apply Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Campus Map Search Clear Search About Directory (opens in new window/tab) myMU (opens in new window/tab) Athletics (opens in new window/tab) Map Jobs at MU Library Virtual Experience (opens in new window/tab) Financial Aid & Tuition Make a Gift Upcoming Events All Events Oct 17 Open House all day Oct 19 Classes Resume; Second Subterm Begins 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 30 PM N/A Oct 26 Advisement Period 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 27 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 28 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 29 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Latest News More News Post RSS Feeds Subscribe to Post Alerts Misericordia University Dean Presents at tecBRIDGE Innovation Conference 9 / 4 / 2026 9 : 26 AM Misericordia University Bridge Program Helps First-Year Students Prepare for College Success 9 / 3 / 2026 1 : 04 PM Misericordia University Expands Nursing Pathways as Pennsylvania Addresses Workforce Shortage 9 / 2 / 2026 10 : 51 AM Misericordia University Celebrates Convocation and Welcomes the Class of 2030 8 / 28 / 2026 2 : 06 PM Misericordia University Professor Selected for UC Berkeley Bridging Differences Fellowship 8 / 13 / 2026 10 : 03 AM Misericordia University Appoints Two New Members to Board of Trustees 7 / 30 / 2026 12 : 09 PM Admissions FAQ's More FAQ's What are the admission requirements? What type of financial aid is available? When should I apply? Who can I contact with questions about my application? What are the admission requirements? MU typically likes to see students with a history of proven success in the classroom with a minimum high school grade point average of 2.5. Minimum *SAT requirement is typically an 850 (Math + Critical Reading), but other factors can be taken into consideration. A number of programs have requirements for direct entry that are higher than university minimums. We advise checking the admission requirements for your program of interest within its designated section of the website. View our list of majors to find your program. *Note: Misericordia will be Test-Optional for Fall 2021 Admissions What type of financial aid is available? Misericordia offers merit-based scholarships for academics as well as community involvement, and need-based awards which can total well over $20,000 per year for qualified students. Visit our Financial Aid page to learn more . When should I apply? MU has a rolling admissions cycle, but we advise that students apply early in the cycle (Fall) as the space available in certain programs can be limited. Visit our Apply page to submit an application . Who can I contact with questions about my application? Your admissions counselor, or the Admissions Office at admiss@misericordia.edu or 1-866-262-6363. View our list of Admissions Staff to find your counselor. Career, Professional Development, & Leadership Mission Statement Our mission is to create inclusive and transformative learning experiences that empower students to thrive in an ever-changing professional world by providing resources, cultivating leadership, and developing the skills needed for professional success. We aim to foster lifelong professional growth through intentional support and meaningful opportunities. Office & Staff Insalaco Center for Professional Development and Leadership McAuley Hall 1st Floor, Room 106 301 Lake Street, Dallas, PA 18612 570-674-6409 | iccareer@misericordia.edu Office Hours: Monday through Friday 8:30 - 4:30 (4:00 May 11 - Aug 18) Bernadette (Bernie) Rushmer Director, Professional Development and Leadership 570-674-8028 | brushmer@misericordia.edu Tiffany Wiernusz Assistant Director, Professional Development and Leadership 570-674-6343 | twiernusz@misericordia.edu Johnna Evans, M.S. Corporate Relations Coordinator 570-674-6184 | jevans@misericordia.edu Janine Fawbush Administrative Assistant 570-674-6409 | jfawbush@misericordia.edu Career Center Spotlight See what’s happening at the Insalaco Center for Professional Development and Leadership. @misericordiau @Archie McGrowl stopped by the MU Career Center to get a new fit, develop a resume, mock interview and a new headshot #archie #archiemcgrowl #mistok #misericordiauniversity #mucareercenter #careers #mascottiktok #collegemascot ♬ original sound - Misericordia University Career & Networking Fairs Upcoming Fairs Fall 2026 Healthcare Career & Networking Fair - Friday, November 13, 2026 - 11:00am - 1:30pm Spring 2027 Career & Networking Fair - Friday, March 19, 2027 - 11:00am - 1:30pm More details can be found on Handshake . On-Campus Recruiting Options If you are interested in hosting an information table, an information session, or participating in on-campus interviews, please reach out to Janine Fawbush at jfawbush@misericordia.edu for more details. Healthcare Career Fair Highlights Check out our previous Healthcare Career Fair and see how students connected with employers and explored career pathways. Jobs and Internships Post on Handshake or attend recruitment events. Guaranteed Placement Program and Career Readiness Click for Career & Grad School Readiness Program Parent Information Help your student on the path to success! Student Government Association Misericordia SGA: Student-run board representing university students. Graduate School Resources Graduate and professional school assistance can be found here! Upcoming Events Click here Alumni on LinkedIn Click Here Career Outcomes Click Here Featured News Misericordia University Students Attend Family Service Association National Family Week Conference Dec 1 2025 9 : 37 AM Misericordia’s Insalaco Center for Professional Development and Leadership sponsored four students to attend the Family Service Association’s National Family Week Conference on November 7. Read More about Misericordia University Students Attend Family Service Association National Family Week Conference University News & Happenings Post RSS Feeds Subscribe to Post Alerts Misericordia University Dean Presents at tecBRIDGE Innovation Conference Sep 4 2026 9 : 26 AM Read More about Misericordia University Dean Presents at tecBRIDGE Innovation Conference Misericordia University Bridge Program Helps First-Year Students Prepare for College Success Sep 3 2026 1 : 04 PM Read More about Misericordia University Bridge Program Helps First-Year Students Prepare for College Success Misericordia University Expands Nursing Pathways as Pennsylvania Addresses Workforce Shortage Sep 2 2026 10 : 51 AM Read More about Misericordia University Expands Nursing Pathways as Pennsylvania Addresses Workforce Shortage Misericordia University Celebrates Convocation and Welcomes the Class of 2030 Aug 28 2026 2 : 06 PM Read More about Misericordia University Celebrates Convocation and Welcomes the Class of 2030 Misericordia University Professor Selected for UC Berkeley Bridging Differences Fellowship Aug 13 2026 10 : 03 AM Read More about Misericordia University Professor Selected for UC Berkeley Bridging Differences Fellowship Misericordia University Appoints Two New Members to Board of Trustees Jul 30 2026 12 : 09 PM Read More about Misericordia University Appoints Two New Members to Board of Trustees Misericordia University Physical Therapy Students Promote Healthy Aging Through Community Mobility Clinic Jul 29 2026 9 : 22 AM Read More about Misericordia University Physical Therapy Students Promote Healthy Aging Through Community Mobility Clinic Misericordia University Helps Radiologic Technologists Advance Their Careers Through Offering a 12-month Online Radiation Therapy Certificate Program Jul 23 2026 9 : 36 AM Read More about Misericordia University Helps Radiologic Technologists Advance Their Careers Through Offering a 12-month Online Radiation Therapy Certificate Program Misericordia University Students Earn National Honors at FBLA Collegiate National Leadership Conference Jul 14 2026 11 : 50 AM Read More about Misericordia University Students Earn National Honors at FBLA Collegiate National Leadership Conference Misericordia University Women with Children Program Featured at Pennsylvania State of the Woman Listening Session Jul 13 2026 11 : 22 AM Read More about Misericordia University Women with Children Program Featured at Pennsylvania State of the Woman Listening Session Misericordia University Occupational Therapy Faculty, Students Present Research at National Conference Jul 8 2026 9 : 22 AM Read More about Misericordia University Occupational Therapy Faculty, Students Present Research at National Conference Misericordia Speech-Language Pathology Student Kara Thourot Earns Pennsylvania Von Drach Memorial Scholarship Jul 7 2026 9 : 20 AM Read More about Misericordia Speech-Language Pathology Student Kara Thourot Earns Pennsylvania Von Drach Memorial Scholarship Misericordia University Students Earn Top Honors at Pennsylvania Academy of Science's 101st Annual Meeting Jun 25 2026 1 : 23 PM Read More about Misericordia University Students Earn Top Honors at Pennsylvania Academy of Science's 101st Annual Meeting Misericordia University Faculty Member Presents Research at International Business History Conference in London Jun 18 2026 12 : 00 PM Read More about Misericordia University Faculty Member Presents Research at International Business History Conference in London Misericordia University Receives $200,000 State Grant to Support Women with Children Program Jun 10 2026 2 : 23 PM Read More about Misericordia University Receives $200,000 State Grant to Support Women with Children Program < > See More News Misericordia University Founded by the Sisters of Mercy 301 Lake Street, Dallas , PA 18612 (570) 674-6400 Helpful Links Full-Time Undergraduate Online Programs Accelerated Degrees Jobs at MU Part-Time Graduate Open Houses Ma