tors can be taken into consideration. A number of programs have requirements for direct entry that are higher than university minimums. We advise checking the admission requirements for your program of interest within its designated section of the website. View our list of majors to find your program. *Note: Misericordia will be Test-Optional for Fall 2021 Admissions What type of financial aid is available? Misericordia offers merit-based scholarships for academics as well as community involvement, and need-based awards which can total well over $20,000 per year for qualified students. Visit our Financial Aid page to learn more . When should I apply? MU has a rolling admissions cycle, but we advise that students apply early in the cycle (Fall) as the space available in certain programs can be limited. Visit our Apply page to submit an application . Who can I contact with questions about my application? Your admissions counselor, or the Admissions Office at admiss@misericordia.edu or 1-866-262-6363. View our list of Admissions Staff to find your counselor. Residence Hall Opening & Closing Below are the dates that the residence halls on Misericordia's campus will close and require all students to depart. Some students through approval from the Campus Life Office will be permit to remain. All closing information will be delivered through email. Students will be required to complete our departure scheduler stating the time they will be leaving for a break and confirm them have left through that scheduler. Information concerning applying for Break Housing will be delivered through those closing information emails. Fall 2025 Thanksgiving Break Winter Break (end of the Fall 2025 semester) Thanksgiving Break The Residence Halls will close for Thanksgiving on Wednesday, Nov. 26th, 2025 at 9am . All students not permitted to stay will be required to leave by that time. The Residence Halls will reopen on Sunday, Nov. 30th, 2025 at Noon. Please do not return prior to that time. Winter Break (end of the Fall 2025 semester) The Residence Halls will close on Saturday, Dec. 13th, 2025 at 3pm . All students not permitted to stay will be required to leave by that time. Checkout Scheduler with closing information will be emailed to all students no later than the end of the day, Dec. 1st, 2025. Any students needing to stay during the break will need to apply for Break Housing and will only be permitted for academic or university related purposes. The Athletic Department will provide Campus Life with any athletes that are permitted to stay during Winter Break. Spring 2026 Spring 2026 Opening Spring Break Easter End of the Year Spring 2026 Opening The Residence Halls will open for the Spring 2026 semester on Sunday, January 11th, 2026 at Noon. This opening is for all returning students an new admits for the spring semester. Please report to the residence halls you are assign. Anyone returning prior to Jan. 11th, 2025 must receive permission from the Campus Life Office. You can request permission by emailing campuslife@misericordia.edu. The Athletic Department will provide a list to Campus Life of the athletes that are permitted to return to campus early. Spring Break The Residence Halls will close for Spring Break on Friday, February 27th, 2026 at 5pm . All students not permitted to stay will be required to leave by that time. Any students needing to stay during the break will need to apply for Break Housing and will only be permitted for academic or university related purposes. The Athletic Department will provide Campus Life with any athletes that are permitted to stay during Winter Break. The Residence Halls will reopen on Sunday, March 8th, 2026 at Noon . Please do not return prior to that time. Easter The university will not close the Residence Halls for Easter Break for the Spring 2026 semester. End of the Year The Residence Halls will close for the 2025-2026 academic year on Friday, May 8th, 2026 at Noon . All students will need to depart at that time. Please make your travel plans accordingly. Any students needing to stay during after closing will  will only be permitted for academic or university related purposes such as graduation. The Athletic Department will provide Campus Life with any athletes that are permitted to after closing due to postseason competition. Students will receive their closing instructions via email no later than the end of the day Friday, April 24th, 2026. Please read all instructions and complete the checkout scheduler allowing the Campus Life Staff to know when you plan to depart. Misericordia University Founded by the Sisters of Mercy 301 Lake Street, Dallas , PA 18612 (570) 674-6400 Helpful Links Full-Time Undergraduate Online Programs Accelerated Degrees Jobs at MU Part-Time Graduate Open Houses Make a Gift to MU TikTok (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) Facebook (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) LinkedIn (opens in new window/tab) Privacy Policy (opens in new window/tab) Site Map Accessibility Back to top Powered by Finalsite"
