s & Centers Campus Store University Camps Other Offices Athletics Information For Future Students Parents and Families ROTC & Veterans Alumni (opens in new window/tab) Corporate Sponsors Donors Print Find It Fast Panel Close Panel Visit Apply Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Campus Map Search Clear Search About Directory (opens in new window/tab) myMU (opens in new window/tab) Athletics (opens in new window/tab) Map Jobs at MU Library Virtual Experience (opens in new window/tab) Financial Aid & Tuition Make a Gift Upcoming Events All Events Oct 17 Open House all day Oct 19 Classes Resume; Second Subterm Begins 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 30 PM N/A Oct 26 Advisement Period 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 27 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 28 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 29 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Latest News More News Post RSS Feeds Subscribe to Post Alerts Misericordia University Dean Presents at tecBRIDGE Innovation Conference 9 / 4 / 2026 9 : 26 AM Misericordia University Bridge Program Helps First-Year Students Prepare for College Success 9 / 3 / 2026 1 : 04 PM Misericordia University Expands Nursing Pathways as Pennsylvania Addresses Workforce Shortage 9 / 2 / 2026 10 : 51 AM Misericordia University Celebrates Convocation and Welcomes the Class of 2030 8 / 28 / 2026 2 : 06 PM Misericordia University Professor Selected for UC Berkeley Bridging Differences Fellowship 8 / 13 / 2026 10 : 03 AM Misericordia University Appoints Two New Members to Board of Trustees 7 / 30 / 2026 12 : 09 PM Admissions FAQ's More FAQ's What are the admission requirements? What type of financial aid is available? When should I apply? Who can I contact with questions about my application? What are the admission requirements? MU typically likes to see students with a history of proven success in the classroom with a minimum high school grade point average of 2.5. Minimum *SAT requirement is typically an 850 (Math + Critical Reading), but other factors can be taken into consideration. A number of programs have requirements for direct entry that are higher than university minimums. We advise checking the admission requirements for your program of interest within its designated section of the website. View our list of majors to find your program. *Note: Misericordia will be Test-Optional for Fall 2021 Admissions What type of financial aid is available? Misericordia offers merit-based scholarships for academics as well as community involvement, and need-based awards which can total well over $20,000 per year for qualified students. Visit our Financial Aid page to learn more . When should I apply? MU has a rolling admissions cycle, but we advise that students apply early in the cycle (Fall) as the space available in certain programs can be limited. Visit our Apply page to submit an application . Who can I contact with questions about my application? Your admissions counselor, or the Admissions Office at admiss@misericordia.edu or 1-866-262-6363. View our list of Admissions Staff to find your counselor. Misericordia University Student Government Association Student Leadership Student Government Association The official voice of Misericordia University students—advocating for a stronger, more connected campus community. Watch: SGA at Misericordia Learn how SGA advocates for students, supports campus organizations, and helps shape student life through leadership,\n            collaboration, and service. Explore Student Clubs & Intramurals Our Purpose The Student Government Association (SGA) of Misericordia University is the official voice of the student body,\n          dedicated to enhancing the campus living and learning experience. SGA listens to student concerns and advocates directly with\n          University leadership to ensure student perspectives are heard and valued. As a student-run, student-elected organization , SGA represents students on University committees and serves as\n          the governing body for campus clubs and organizations. Through leadership, collaboration, and advocacy, SGA supports student\n          involvement across campus. Guided by Misericordia’s core values of mercy , service , justice , and hospitality , SGA is committed to serving students and strengthening a vibrant, inclusive campus community. What SGA Does Advocates for Students Brings student concerns and ideas to University leadership. Represents Student Voices Serves on committees to help shape campus life. Supports Clubs & Organizations Guides and strengthens student involvement across campus. Contact SGA SGA in Action Highlights from Student Government Association events and campus activities. ❮ ❯ 2025–2026 SGA Executive Board Student leaders representing the Misericordia University student body and supporting campus involvement. Executive Board President Ruth “Camille” Mann Vice President Adithya Hanakere Virupakasha Treasurer Connor McGee Administrative Coordinator Keira McCaffrey University Policy Liaison Isabelle Romano Advisors Bernie Rushmer, Valerie Bildheiser, Amy Lahart Contact Email Student Government Misericordia University Banks Student Life Center, Room 132 301 Lake Street Dallas, PA 18612-1098 For questions about clubs and organizations, email sgovern@misericordia.edu . Misericordia University Founded by the Sisters of Mercy 301 Lake Street, Dallas , PA 18612 (570) 674-6400 Helpful Links Full-Time Undergraduate Online Programs Accelerated Degrees Jobs at MU Part-Time Graduate Open Houses Make a Gift to MU TikTok (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) Facebook (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) LinkedIn (opens in new window/tab) Privacy Policy (opens in new window/tab) Site Map Accessibility Back to top Powered by Finalsite"
    },
