& Centers Campus Store University Camps Other Offices Athletics Information For Future Students Parents and Families ROTC & Veterans Alumni (opens in new window/tab) Corporate Sponsors Donors Print Find It Fast Panel Close Panel Visit Apply Request Info (opens in new window/tab) Campus Map Search Clear Search About Directory (opens in new window/tab) myMU (opens in new window/tab) Athletics (opens in new window/tab) Map Jobs at MU Library Virtual Experience (opens in new window/tab) Financial Aid & Tuition Make a Gift Upcoming Events All Events Oct 17 Open House all day Oct 19 Classes Resume; Second Subterm Begins 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 30 PM N/A Oct 26 Advisement Period 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 27 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 28 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 29 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Latest News More News Post RSS Feeds Subscribe to Post Alerts Misericordia University Dean Presents at tecBRIDGE Innovation Conference 9 / 4 / 2026 9 : 26 AM Misericordia University Bridge Program Helps First-Year Students Prepare for College Success 9 / 3 / 2026 1 : 04 PM Misericordia University Expands Nursing Pathways as Pennsylvania Addresses Workforce Shortage 9 / 2 / 2026 10 : 51 AM Misericordia University Celebrates Convocation and Welcomes the Class of 2030 8 / 28 / 2026 2 : 06 PM Misericordia University Professor Selected for UC Berkeley Bridging Differences Fellowship 8 / 13 / 2026 10 : 03 AM Misericordia University Appoints Two New Members to Board of Trustees 7 / 30 / 2026 12 : 09 PM Admissions FAQ's More FAQ's What are the admission requirements? What type of financial aid is available? When should I apply? Who can I contact with questions about my application? What are the admission requirements? MU typically likes to see students with a history of proven success in the classroom with a minimum high school grade point average of 2.5. Minimum *SAT requirement is typically an 850 (Math + Critical Reading), but other factors can be taken into consideration. A number of programs have requirements for direct entry that are higher than university minimums. We advise checking the admission requirements for your program of interest within its designated section of the website. View our list of majors to find your program. *Note: Misericordia will be Test-Optional for Fall 2021 Admissions What type of financial aid is available? Misericordia offers merit-based scholarships for academics as well as community involvement, and need-based awards which can total well over $20,000 per year for qualified students. Visit our Financial Aid page to learn more . When should I apply? MU has a rolling admissions cycle, but we advise that students apply early in the cycle (Fall) as the space available in certain programs can be limited. Visit our Apply page to submit an application . Who can I contact with questions about my application? Your admissions counselor, or the Admissions Office at admiss@misericordia.edu or 1-866-262-6363. View our list of Admissions Staff to find your counselor. Graduate & Professional School Resources The Insalaco Center for Professional Development and Leadership can help you prepare for this important step in your academic career of applying to graduate or professional school. A number of useful resources are available on campus and online for individuals considering applying to graduate or professional school.  Contact us to schedule an appointment to: Discuss career goals and objectives Research and obtain more information about specific programs of interests Identify and discuss other factors that might help to determine where to apply, such as size of the institution, geographic location, student life, financial aid, etc. Determine if an entrance exam is required for admission and review available test locations, dates and times Schedule a free practice test Review personal statements, CV/resumes, and related materials to ensure goals and experiences are well represented within the application Prepare for a graduate school interview with a mock interview If you are a student and would like to schedule an appointment to discuss the graduate/professional school path, contact Tiffany Wiernusz, Assistant Director, at twiernusz@misericordia.edu for an appointment. Misericordia University Founded by the Sisters of Mercy 301 Lake Street, Dallas , PA 18612 (570) 674-6400 Helpful Links Full-Time Undergraduate Online Programs Accelerated Degrees Jobs at MU Part-Time Graduate Open Houses Make a Gift to MU TikTok (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) Facebook (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) LinkedIn (opens in new window/tab) Privacy Policy (opens in new window/tab) Site Map Accessibility Back to top Powered by Finalsite"
