se all day Oct 19 Classes Resume; Second Subterm Begins 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 30 PM N/A Oct 26 Advisement Period 7 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 27 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 28 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Oct 29 Advisement Period 12 : 00 AM - 11 : 59 PM N/A Latest News More News Post RSS Feeds Subscribe to Post Alerts Misericordia University Dean Presents at tecBRIDGE Innovation Conference 9 / 4 / 2026 9 : 26 AM Misericordia University Bridge Program Helps First-Year Students Prepare for College Success 9 / 3 / 2026 1 : 04 PM Misericordia University Expands Nursing Pathways as Pennsylvania Addresses Workforce Shortage 9 / 2 / 2026 10 : 51 AM Misericordia University Celebrates Convocation and Welcomes the Class of 2030 8 / 28 / 2026 2 : 06 PM Misericordia University Professor Selected for UC Berkeley Bridging Differences Fellowship 8 / 13 / 2026 10 : 03 AM Misericordia University Appoints Two New Members to Board of Trustees 7 / 30 / 2026 12 : 09 PM Admissions FAQ's More FAQ's What are the admission requirements? What type of financial aid is available? When should I apply? Who can I contact with questions about my application? What are the admission requirements? MU typically likes to see students with a history of proven success in the classroom with a minimum high school grade point average of 2.5. Minimum *SAT requirement is typically an 850 (Math + Critical Reading), but other factors can be taken into consideration. A number of programs have requirements for direct entry that are higher than university minimums. We advise checking the admission requirements for your program of interest within its designated section of the website. View our list of majors to find your program. *Note: Misericordia will be Test-Optional for Fall 2021 Admissions What type of financial aid is available? Misericordia offers merit-based scholarships for academics as well as community involvement, and need-based awards which can total well over $20,000 per year for qualified students. Visit our Financial Aid page to learn more . When should I apply? MU has a rolling admissions cycle, but we advise that students apply early in the cycle (Fall) as the space available in certain programs can be limited. Visit our Apply page to submit an application . Who can I contact with questions about my application? Your admissions counselor, or the Admissions Office at admiss@misericordia.edu or 1-866-262-6363. View our list of Admissions Staff to find your counselor. Employment Opportunities Our Human Resources Department engages in a host of service activities such as recruiting and hiring new employees, administering benefits, planning and conducting training programs, serving as in-house consultant to supervisors and employees, and employee relations. Misericordia University is an equal opportunity employer. Misericordia University does not discriminate in employment and no question during the application process is used for the purpose of limiting or excluding any applicant's consideration for employment on a basis prohibited by local, state or federal law. View Faculty Employment Opportunities View Staff Employment Opportunities View Graduate Assistant Opportunities There are no resources or collections to display Information Technology (opens in new window/tab) Human Resources Compliance Corner ACT 153 - Contact With Minors on Campus Benefit Notices Summary Annual Reports Summary Plan Descriptions Employment Opportunities Faculty Employee Opportunities Staff Employment Opportunities Graduate Assistant  Employment Opportunities xxStaff Employment Opportunities  clone xxGraduate Assistant  Employment Opportunities clone Office of Sponsored Research Institutional Review Board (opens in new window/tab) Office of Institutional Research Institutional Research Common Data Set Fact Book Quick Facts Student Achievements Data Schedule Data Requests Dashboards Surveys CESS Surveys NSSE Surveys Accreditations Resources Marketing 