isericordia University Celebrates Convocation and Welcomes the Class of 2030 8 / 28 / 2026 2 : 06 PM Misericordia University Professor Selected for UC Berkeley Bridging Differences Fellowship 8 / 13 / 2026 10 : 03 AM Misericordia University Appoints Two New Members to Board of Trustees 7 / 30 / 2026 12 : 09 PM Admissions FAQ's More FAQ's What are the admission requirements? What type of financial aid is available? When should I apply? Who can I contact with questions about my application? What are the admission requirements? MU typically likes to see students with a history of proven success in the classroom with a minimum high school grade point average of 2.5. Minimum *SAT requirement is typically an 850 (Math + Critical Reading), but other factors can be taken into consideration. A number of programs have requirements for direct entry that are higher than university minimums. We advise checking the admission requirements for your program of interest within its designated section of the website. View our list of majors to find your program. *Note: Misericordia will be Test-Optional for Fall 2021 Admissions What type of financial aid is available? Misericordia offers merit-based scholarships for academics as well as community involvement, and need-based awards which can total well over $20,000 per year for qualified students. Visit our Financial Aid page to learn more . When should I apply? MU has a rolling admissions cycle, but we advise that students apply early in the cycle (Fall) as the space available in certain programs can be limited. Visit our Apply page to submit an application . Who can I contact with questions about my application? Your admissions counselor, or the Admissions Office at admiss@misericordia.edu or 1-866-262-6363. View our list of Admissions Staff to find your counselor. Misericordia University Professor Selected for UC Berkeley Bridging Differences Fellowship Post RSS Feeds Subscribe to Post Alerts Misericordia University Professor Selected for UC Berkeley Bridging Differences Fellowship 8 / 13 / 2026 10 : 03 AM Nordstrom Selected for UC Berkeley Fellowship on Bridging Differences in Higher Education DALLAS, Pa. — Alicia Nordstrom, Ph.D., professor of psychology at Misericordia University, has been selected to participate in the Bridging Differences in Higher Education Learning Fellowship , an eight-month program hosted by the Greater Good Science Center at the University of California, Berkeley. Nordstrom was selected for the fellowship’s Project-Based Cohort, a group of 25 higher education faculty, administrators and staff committed to developing initiatives that foster constructive dialogue and deeper understanding across differences on college campuses. Fellows receive professional development, skills-building opportunities and ongoing support as they develop or strengthen projects at their institutions. Nordstrom has participated in the Bridging Differences in Higher Education program for the past three years. Her work focuses on helping students develop skills for respectful dialogue, perspective-taking and engagement with challenging topics. “I have participated in the Bridging Differences in Higher Education program for the past three years and am so honored to be selected for this fellowship program,” Nordstrom said. “This program brings together educators who share the goal of helping students develop the skills needed for respectful and engaging dialogue about difficult topics and a meaningful exchange of ideas.” Nordstrom said one of the most valuable lessons of the program is learning to approach disagreement with curiosity rather than persuasion. “One of the most important skills is to focus on listening and understanding, not persuading,” she said. “Once you let go of trying to convince someone else that you are ‘right,’ you are better able to see another person as someone who has beliefs and wants to be heard and understood.” Through the fellowship, Nordstrom will collaborate with educators from other institutions while developing a project designed to strengthen Misericordia University’s efforts to encourage constructive dialogue and bridge differences across perspectives. Share to Facebook Share to Twitter Share to LinkedIn Share to Pinterest Share to Email Print this page More News Stories Post RSS Feeds Subscribe to Post Alerts Play and Pause Buttons for Slideshow pause play Misericordia University Dean Presents at tecBRIDGE Innovation Conference Madonna Mantione Read More about Misericordia University Dean Presents at tecBRIDGE Innovation Conference Misericordia University Bridge Program Helps First-Year Students Prepare for College Success Madonna Mantione Read More about Misericordia University Bridge Program Helps First-Year Students Prepare for College Success Misericordia University Expands Nursing Pathways as Pennsylvania Addresses Workforce Shortage Madonna Mantione Read More about Misericordia University Expands Nursing Pathways as Pennsylvania Addresses Workforce Shortage Misericordia University Celebrates Convocation and Welcomes the Class of 2030 Madonna Mantione Read More about Misericordia University Celebrates Convocation and Welcomes the Class of 2030 Misericordia University Professor Selected for UC Berkeley Bridging Differences Fellowship Madonna Mantione Read More about Misericordia University Professor Selected for UC Berkeley Bridging Differences Fellowship Misericordia University Appoints Two New Members to Board of Trustees Madonna Mantione Read More about Misericordia University Appoints Two New Members to Board of Trustees < > Back to News Misericordia University Founded by the Sisters of Mercy 301 Lake Street, Dallas , PA 18612 (570) 674-6400 Helpful Links Full-Time Undergraduate Online Programs Accelerated Degrees Jobs at MU Part-Time Graduate Open Houses Make a Gift to MU TikTok (opens in new window/tab) Instagram (opens in new window/tab) Facebook (opens in new window/tab) YouTube (opens in new window/tab) Linked